<task id="001" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Shared RecordCommandBar + record-action icon map (FR-04, FR-05)</title>
    <phase>1 Record template and actions</phase>
    <gate>startable after the owner reviews the plan and tasks (owner directive 2026-11-10)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Creates new .tsx/.ts files in the shared library (tags frontend, fluent-ui; code implementation)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>New shared pattern/abstraction under an approved ADR-012 Path C tension; needs code-review + adr-check sign-off</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, react, typescript, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add a shared, data-free `RecordCommandBar` to `@spaarke/ui-components` that renders record-level actions from descriptors (hidden actions are not rendered at all), composing `HeaderToolbar`, plus one exported icon-map constant for record actions. The external SPA's record template (task 003) consumes it for every record toolbar.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Fluent UI v9, React and shared-library design (ADR-012, ADR-021). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordCommandBar/` exists with the component, its exported types, the icon map constant, an index, and Jest tests; it is exported from `src/components/index.ts`; a candidate second consumer is named with file evidence in the task notes and the PR; code-review and adr-check approve the shared placement explicitly.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-04/FR-05 and §ADR Tensions (ADR-012 Path C, owner 2026-11-08). Design §6 holds the icon table (icons verified present 2026-10-21). The prototype `c:\code_files\spaarke-prototype\projects\2026-10-spa-record-modal\src\template\RecordToolbar.tsx` is the visual reference only (labelled buttons); the spec contract (tooltip = aria-label, HeaderToolbar composition) wins.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordCommandBar/RecordCommandBar.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordCommandBar/types.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordCommandBar/recordActionIcons.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordCommandBar/index.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordCommandBar/__tests__/RecordCommandBar.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/index.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/HeaderToolbar/HeaderToolbar.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/HeaderToolbar/types.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/HeaderToolbar/README.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/HeaderToolbar/__tests__/HeaderToolbar.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/CommandBar.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/EmailReadingPaneShell/EmailToolbar.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">`RecordCommandBar` (every file under `components/RecordCommandBar/`) has no `Xrm`, no `ComponentFramework`, no data fetching, no `fetch`/`authenticatedFetch`, and no entity-name literals (`sprk_*`, "matter", "project", …). Its prop and descriptor types are exported from its index and the components barrel.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012 Path C (spec §ADR Tensions)">It composes `HeaderToolbar` (each visible, non-overflow action becomes an `IHeaderToolbarSlot`) and Fluent v9 primitives; it does not copy HeaderToolbar's button/tooltip markup. If review rejects shared placement, it falls back to SPA-local and the owner is told — do not decide that yourself.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-04">The action descriptor fields are exactly: `id`, `label`, `icon`, `onClick`, `visible`, `tooltip`, optional `overflow`. There is no `disabled` field (hide, don't disable — owner 2026-11-08). An action with `visible === false` is not rendered: not in the DOM, no tab stop.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-05">The icon map is ONE exported constant (`RECORD_ACTION_ICONS`) keyed by action id: refresh `ArrowClockwise20Regular`, upload `ArrowUpload20Regular`, newMessage `ChatAdd20Regular`, addTodo `TaskListAdd20Regular`, addEvent `CalendarAdd20Regular`, submitInvoice `ReceiptAdd20Regular`, copyLink `Link20Regular`, expandSection `Open20Regular`, download `ArrowDownload20Regular`, delete `Delete20Regular`, history `History20Regular`, send `Send20Regular`, all from `@fluentui/react-icons`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Every style in the new files uses Fluent v9 semantic tokens via `makeStyles`; no hex/rgb/hsl literals. Works in light, dark and high-contrast.</constraint>
    <constraint source="src/client/shared/CLAUDE.md">Export from the main barrel only (`src/components/index.ts`); do not add it to `pcf-safe.ts`. Use only React 16/17-safe APIs (as HeaderToolbar does) so a PCF-hosted consumer can adopt it later. No new npm dependency.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not change `HeaderToolbar`'s public contract (`IHeaderToolbarSlot`, `IHeaderToolbarProps`) — its types file says changes are breaking. Do not migrate any existing toolbar in this task.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/design.md</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-react-version-boundaries.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md</file>
