    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="HeaderToolbar slot composition" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/HeaderToolbar/HeaderToolbar.tsx">Icon-only Button inside Tooltip relationship="label", aria-label = tooltip; `buttonRef` anchors a popover — use it to anchor the overflow Menu.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Overflow menu" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/commandBar/CommandBar.tsx">`renderOverflowMenu` (Menu/MenuTrigger/MenuPopover/MenuList) — the overflow interaction to mirror.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Write `types.ts`: `RecordCommandBarAction` (the FR-04 fields only) and `RecordCommandBarProps` (`actions`, `ariaLabel`, optional `className`). JSDoc every public prop.</step>
    <step order="2">Write `recordActionIcons.ts`: the `RECORD_ACTION_ICONS` constant and its key type `RecordActionIconId`.</step>
    <step order="3">Write `RecordCommandBar.tsx`: filter `visible`, map non-overflow actions to HeaderToolbar slots (tooltip = the action's tooltip), and render overflow actions in a Fluent v9 Menu behind one "More actions" slot that appears only when at least one visible action has `overflow: true`.</step>
    <step order="4">Write `index.ts` and add `export * from './RecordCommandBar';` to `src/components/index.ts` next to the HeaderToolbar export.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the Jest tests (React Testing Library inside `FluentProvider`), then run `npm test -- RecordCommandBar` and the package type check/build in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components`.</step>
    <step order="6">Name the candidate second consumer with file evidence in `projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-001-notes.md` (start from `EmailToolbar.tsx`, see notes); copy it into the PR description.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `/code-review` and `/adr-check` on the change; record their explicit Path C approval (or rejection) in the task notes. On rejection, STOP (escalation).</step>
    <step order="8">Run tests and verify all pass.</step>
    <step order="9">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="10">Record deviations and decisions in `projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-001-notes.md`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If overflow or keyboard behaviour cannot be built without changing HeaderToolbar's public types, STOP and escalate (root CLAUDE.md §6: breaking shared-lib contract) rather than editing HeaderToolbar.</trigger>
    <trigger>If code-review or adr-check rejects the shared placement, STOP: report to the owner with the SPA-local fallback (spec §ADR Tensions); do not move the component yourself.</trigger>
    <trigger>If an icon in FR-05 is missing from the installed `@fluentui/react-icons`, STOP and report it; do not substitute another icon.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`HeaderToolbar` (components/HeaderToolbar/HeaderToolbar.tsx:134, section-card header icon slots), `DocumentToolbar` (components/DocumentToolbar/DocumentToolbar.tsx:105, document-grid actions with disabled states), `DataGrid/commandBar/CommandBar.tsx:310` (grid-scoped, registry-driven) — none renders record-level actions from visibility descriptors.</existing>
    <extension>No as a direct extension: HeaderToolbar's slot contract is frozen (types.ts says changes are breaking) and has no visibility/overflow concept, and DocumentToolbar is document-specific with disabled-not-hidden semantics. RecordCommandBar composes HeaderToolbar instead of extending it.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Each of the six SPA record types hand-builds its toolbar visibility, overflow and icons, so hide-don't-disable drifts per type and a View-only caller can be offered an action that answers 403 (FR-06, NFR-04).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Hidden actions are absent">
      <steps><step>Render RecordCommandBar with refresh (visible), upload (visible=false), copyLink (visible).</step><step>Inspect the DOM and Tab through the bar.</step></steps>
      <expected>No upload button exists in the DOM; Tab visits only Refresh and Copy link.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Overflow menu">
      <steps><step>Render with two visible overflow actions.</step><step>Activate "More actions" with Enter; arrow to the second item; press Enter; press Esc on a reopened menu.</step></steps>
      <expected>The menu opens, the item's onClick fires once, Esc closes the menu and returns focus to the trigger.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode and High Contrast (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Render inside FluentProvider with webDarkTheme, then teamsHighContrastTheme.</step><step>Verify no hard-coded colours; icons use currentColor.</step></steps>
      <expected>All colours come from Fluent v9 semantic tokens; buttons stay visible and focus rings show; no console warnings.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run Jest and the type check in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

