  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an action with `visible: false`, the bar renders no element for it and it gets no tab stop.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every rendered action (inline or in the overflow menu) has a tooltip whose text is also its accessible name (aria-label); a test asserts it for inline and overflow actions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Overflow actions render only inside the "More actions" menu; with no visible overflow action, no "More actions" control exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Keyboard: Tab reaches each inline action and the overflow trigger; Enter and Space activate an action; Esc closes the overflow menu and focus returns to its trigger.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With an empty or all-hidden action list the bar renders without error and contains no buttons.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`RECORD_ACTION_ICONS` is exported from the package barrel and holds exactly the twelve FR-05 entries.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`RecordCommandBar`, `RecordCommandBarProps`, `RecordCommandBarAction` and `RECORD_ACTION_ICONS` are importable from `@spaarke/ui-components`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a grep of `components/RecordCommandBar/` finds no `Xrm`, `ComponentFramework`, `fetch(`, `sprk_` or hex colour literal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">It renders correctly in light, dark and high-contrast Fluent themes (test renders it under each theme without error).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">HeaderToolbar's files are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A candidate second consumer is named with file:line evidence in `notes/task-001-notes.md` and the PR.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">code-review and adr-check record explicit approval of the ADR-012 Path C placement in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The package's Jest suite and type check pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract (visibility, tooltip/aria-label, overflow, keyboard, empty list, themes) plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-04, FR-05, §ADR Tensions (ADR-012), Unresolved Question 3 (candidate second consumer). Candidate verified 2026-11-10: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/EmailReadingPaneShell/EmailToolbar.tsx` hand-builds a record-level action bar (a Fluent Toolbar at :99 with icon-only buttons wrapped in per-button Tooltips from :127: Save to SharePoint, Create Event, Create To Do, Link Invoice, Open full form) gated by one `recordActionsDisabled` flag (disable, not hide). It renders inside `EmailWorkspace.tsx`, consumed by the Console (`src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/workspace/WorkspacePane.tsx`) and `src/solutions/EmailPage/src/main.tsx`; its header says it mirrors the `CommunicationActions` PCF bar (`CommunicationActionsApp.tsx:621`), a second hand-built copy. Name it only; migrating it is out of scope. Icon keys are action ids, not entity literals. Shared-lib tests run under Jest.</notes>

